---
title: "SSRM View Subscription"
enterprise: true
---

When a server pushes live updates, sending updates for rows the user cannot see is wasted work. The `viewSubscription` grid option tells your application which loaded rows to subscribe to and unsubscribe from as rows enter and leave the view.

View subscription requires the `ViewSubscriptionModule` and [Row IDs](./server-side-model-configuration/#providing-row-ids). It works the same way as with the Client-Side Row Model, so start with [View Subscription](./data-update-view-subscription/) for:

- [Handlers](./data-update-view-subscription/#handlers): what `subscribeRows` and `unsubscribeRows` receive, and in what order.
- [Lifecycle](./data-update-view-subscription/#lifecycle): starting, pausing and stopping the subscription.
- [Excluded Rows](./data-update-view-subscription/#excluded-rows): rows that are never passed to the handlers.
- [Debouncing](./data-update-view-subscription/#debouncing): waiting for scrolling to stop before calling the handlers.

This page covers what is different with the Server-Side Row Model: rows that load in blocks, group rows loaded from the server, and aggregates the server calculates.

## Loading and Refreshing

A row is subscribed once it is in view and its block has loaded. Loading rows and rows whose block failed to load are never passed to the handlers.

- A [refresh](./server-side-model-updating-refresh/) without a purge keeps the rows whose IDs are unchanged. A kept row stays subscribed, even when its data changes.
- A refresh with `purge: true` unsubscribes every row, then subscribes them again as they reload.
- A row whose ID changes, through a refresh or a [transaction](./server-side-model-updating-transactions/), is unsubscribed with its old ID and subscribed with the new one.
## Row Types

Rows have the same `type` values as with the [Client-Side Row Model](./data-update-view-subscription/#row-types), with these differences:

- `'group'`: a group row the server loaded, with its `data`. [`getRowId`](./server-side-model-configuration/#providing-row-ids) is called for group rows too, so give them an ID from their route.
- `'tree'`: a row in [Tree Data](./server-side-model-tree-data/). `hasChildren` is `true` for expandable rows, and only expandable rows have a `route`.

### Tree Data {% enterpriseIcon /%} {% #tree-data %}

The example below shows a portfolio of regions, sectors and stocks as [Tree Data](./server-side-model-tree-data/), loaded over a simulated websocket that also streams updates for the subscribed rows. Region and sector rows show the total value of their stocks, which the server streams whenever one of those stocks moves. The updates are applied with [Asynchronous Transactions](./server-side-model-updating-transactions/#asynchronous-updates), using each row's `parentKeys` as the route.

- Scrolling, expanding groups and loading blocks produce subscribe and unsubscribe batches.
- **Purge** reloads all rows. The old rows are unsubscribed, and the new rows subscribed as they load.
- With **Subscription active** cleared, rows still load over the socket, but no updates stream.

